// Generated by metaverse-engine/tools/agent-help-build.coax. Regenerate; do not edit.
#load "help-rules.coax";
AGENT_HELP_FIRST :: [4]string.[
"Animation documents\nUse openagents labs anim check PROJECT.alp1 before play or edit.\nThe ALP1 project retains its ALB1 libraries, performances, scene and cut; JSON components alone are not an ALP1 file.\n\nComplete asset-independent scene component (admitted by anim_scene_load):\n{\"schema\":\"anim.scene.v1\",\"name\":\"help-scene\",\"length\":1,\"style\":\"cel\",\"stage\":{\"realm\":\"animation-lab\",\"place\":\"studio\",\"time\":0.8,\"weather\":\"clear\"},\"cast\":[],\"props\":[],\"effects\":[],\"lights\":[],\"cameras\":[{\"name\":\"wide\",\"fov\":0.8,\"focus\":3,\"keys\":[{\"at\":0,\"eye\":[0,2,4],\"look\":[0,1,0],\"cut\":true,\"ease\":0},{\"at\":1,\"eye\":[1,2,4],\"look\":[0,1,0],\"cut\":false,\"ease\":1}]}],\"sounds\":[]}\n\nLengths and key times are seconds; camera fov is radians, focus and positions are metres. Keys strictly increase. Camera focus and stage weather/time remain metadata in the inspection renderer. An edit uses labs anim edit PROJECT.alp1 --say WORDS through the schema-constrained Decisions API, then labs anim check and play. Licensed library bytes remain private and unchanged.\n\nObject topics (use --all for every key, or help field anim.scene.cameras[].fov):\nanim.buffer\nanim.rig\nanim.rig.joints[]\nanim.rig.face_map[]\nanim.rig.face_map[].outputs[]\nanim.rig.sections[]\nanim.rig.morphs[]\nanim.clip\nanim.clip.events[]\nanim.clip.source\nanim.performance\nanim.performance.layers[]\nanim.scene.cast[].path[]\nanim.scene.cameras[]\nanim.scene.cameras[].keys[]\nanim.scene\nanim.scene.stage\nanim.scene.cast[]\nanim.scene.props[]\nanim.scene.effects[]\nanim.scene.lights[]\nanim.scene.lights[].keys[]\nanim.scene.sounds[]\nanim.cut\nanim.cut.shots[]\nanim.legacy-cut\nanim.pose\nanim.pose.joints[]\nanim.pose.face[]\nanim.direction\nanim.direction.confidence\nanim.direct.reply\nanim.direct.request\nanim.unreal.meshes[]\nanim.unreal.animations[]\nanim.unreal.source\n",
"Film capture with today's tools\nThe current capture record drives openagents labs clip: fixed-step WebGPU frames, retained PNGs and H.264 MP4. This is the existing live rendering profile captured offline. F1 accumulation/physical optics, traced film and native three-world qualification remain separate open work; no unsupported quality switch is implied.\n\nComplete working shot, with the local built site served at 127.0.0.1:9377:\nopenagents labs clip http://127.0.0.1:9377/worlds/everglade2 /tmp/help-film.mp4 --size 640x360 --seconds 1 --fps 24 --frames /tmp/help-film-frames --fresh\n\nFrom a repository checkout, serve the built site using:\ncoax/web/serve.sh apps/openagents-web --static --listen 127.0.0.1:9377\nRun that server separately and keep it running during capture. A source checkout must build the selected realm's Wasm/host components first; help does not install assets or build a realm.\n\nInspect one option with help field film.capture.fps; --all lists all current fields. Numeric profile fields:\nwidth: --size; even pixels, WIDTHxHEIGHT; inclusive range 16..7680; default 1280.\nheight: --size; even pixels, WIDTHxHEIGHT; inclusive range 16..7680; default 720.\nfps: --fps; frames per second; inclusive range 1..120; default 30.\nseconds_ms: --seconds; milliseconds internally; CLI takes seconds; inclusive range 1..600000; default 3000.\nskip_ms: --skip; milliseconds internally; CLI takes seconds; inclusive range 0..3600000; default 0.\n\nAlternative sizes: --phone, --square or --vertical, mutually exclusive with --size. --stage NAME appends the named stage to the URL. --eval runs setup once. No capture plays audio on the owner's computer. An OUT.mp4.json sidecar records source/capture identity. Errors use film.capture.FIELD.\nNative F0 frames already written by vk-realm can be reviewed/encoded with coax/web/tool.sh metaverse-engine/tools/film-frames.coax DIR --out OUT.mp4 [--audio WAV]; this does not claim completion of F0's remaining parity/Metal gates.\n",
"Everglade realm edits\nThis is the eg-edit 1 overlay, not a replacement for the designed city or an authority grant. Publishing still requires the server's admin/owner checks and world revision rules. This help performs no publication.\n\nComplete codec example (metres internally; text x/z/lift in centimetres, yaw in degrees, size in percent):\neg-edit 1\nt 0 600 -1200 0 100\n\nThe t row places an item; p SPOT hides a planned person and b BUILDING hides a planned building. Group/lift/tint are optional trailing fields. Decoding is not placement permission: collision/world-boundary checks still apply. --all lists the live item catalogue and fields; help field realm-edit.thing.kind returns one field.\n\nItem catalogue:\n0: crate\n1: barrel\n2: bench\n3: fence\n4: stall\n5: pumpkin\n6: sack\n7: apple crate\n8: carrots\n9: pot\n10: bucket\n11: lantern\n12: cart\n13: vase\n14: table\n15: chair\n16: stool\n17: anvil\n18: cauldron\n19: training dummy\n20: weapon rack\n21: banner\n22: coins\n23: sign\n24: bush\n25: flowers\n26: rock\n27: rock pile\n28: hay pile\n29: stone wall\n30: crops\n31: house\n32: shed\n33: tower\n",
"Character appearance\nCC2 is the existing frozen 56-byte appearance record. It owns choices, not geometry addresses, authority or renderer state. Character Create's SAVE PLAYER publishes the draft; RESET does not overwrite the saved player.\n\nComplete working record for the default Wizard outfit:\nCC202000810001800000000000000000000000000001111000001100\n\nUse /worlds/character-creator to edit and SAVE PLAYER to apply through the existing profile path. This codec example is data, not a new CLI write command. Legacy CC1 is read and migrated; source arrays are runtime-only. Do not reorder or reuse CC2 wardrobe slots. Use help field appearance.eye_color or --all for every saved choice and part.\n\nSaved fields:\nfemale\nworn\npiece\noutfit\nhood\nhair\nbeard\ndye\nskin\nhair_color\neye_color\nvariant\npose\nklass\nlevel\n",
];
